---
import '../../styles/custom.css'
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro"
const title = 'Vectis Mail alternatives — side-by-side comparisons'
const description = 'Side-by-side comparisons of Vectis Mail vs Mailcow, iRedMail, Mail-in-a-Box, SendGrid, and Postmark. Self-hosted vs managed, free vs metered.'
const url = 'https://vectismail.com/alternatives/'
const ogImage = 'https://vectismail.com/og/default.png'
const dateModified = '2026-05-13'

type Alt = {
	href: string
	title: string
	tagline: string
	bullets: string[]
}

const live: Alt[] = [
	{
		href: '/alternatives/mailcow/',
		title: 'vs Mailcow',
		tagline: 'Same self-hosted stack, declarative YAML config, REST API, atomic updates with rollback.',
		bullets: [
			'14 vs 25+ containers by default',
			'Declarative config + 40+ endpoint REST API',
			'Atomic 6-phase updates with auto-rollback',
		],
	},
	{
		href: '/alternatives/sendgrid/',
		title: 'vs SendGrid',
		tagline: 'Same API surface, no per-email pricing. Flat $0–$59/mo covers unlimited sending volume.',
		bullets: [
			'Flat pricing instead of per-email metered billing',
			'Inbound webhooks + sending API in one platform',
			'Self-hosted, your IPs, your reputation',
		],
	},
	{
		href: '/alternatives/iredmail/',
		title: 'vs iRedMail',
		tagline: 'Compared with the long-running OS-native open-source mail stack: REST API, declarative YAML, Rspamd by default.',
		bullets: [
			'OS-native (iRedMail) vs Docker Compose (Vectis)',
			'Classic mail server vs 40+ endpoint REST API',
			'SpamAssassin default vs Rspamd by default',
		],
	},
	{
		href: '/alternatives/mail-in-a-box/',
		title: 'vs Mail-in-a-Box',
		tagline: 'One-command personal email sovereignty vs API-first multi-tenant infrastructure. When each is the right fit.',
		bullets: [
			'Single-org one-command install vs multi-tenant + API',
			'Bundled CalDAV/CardDAV vs Phase-4 roadmap',
			'CC0 public domain vs BSL 1.1 + commercial Pro',
		],
	},
	{
		href: '/alternatives/postmark/',
		title: 'vs Postmark',
		tagline: 'Flat $0–59/mo self-host vs the developer-loved transactional SaaS. Same API surfaces, mailbox hosting included, cost crossover at ~37K emails/mo.',
		bullets: [
			'Flat-price self-host vs per-email after the 10K base bucket',
			'Mailbox hosting included vs send + inbound parse only',
			'No Message Streams equivalent (gap called out explicitly)',
		],
	},
]

const upcoming: { title: string; tagline: string }[] = []
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
	<title>{title}</title>
	<meta name="description" content={description} />

	<link rel="canonical" href={url} />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32" />

	<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
	<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
	<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
	<meta property="og:url" content={url} />
	<meta property="og:image" content={ogImage} />
	<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
	<meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
	<meta property="og:image:alt" content="Vectis Mail alternatives — side-by-side comparisons" />
	<meta property="og:site_name" content="Vectis Mail" />

	<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
	<meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
	<meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
	<meta name="twitter:image" content={ogImage} />

	<meta name="theme-color" content="#0C0C0D" />

	<script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@graph": [
			{
				"@type": "BreadcrumbList",
				"itemListElement": [
					{ "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Vectis Mail", "item": "https://vectismail.com/" },
					{ "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Alternatives", "item": url }
				]
			},
			{
				"@type": "CollectionPage",
				"@id": url + "#page",
				"name": title,
				"description": description,
				"url": url,
				"isPartOf": { "@type": "WebSite", "name": "Vectis Mail", "url": "https://vectismail.com/" },
				"mainEntity": {
					"@type": "ItemList",
					"itemListElement": live.map((a, i) => ({
						"@type": "ListItem",
						"position": i + 1,
						"url": "https://vectismail.com" + a.href,
						"name": a.title,
					})),
				},
			},
			{
				"@type": "FAQPage",
				"mainEntity": [
					{
						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "Which Vectis Mail alternative comparison should I read first?",
						"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Start with the comparison that matches what you're running today. If you operate a Mailcow stack and want a more declarative surface, read /alternatives/mailcow/. If you're paying SendGrid or Postmark per email and want flat pricing on a self-hosted stack, read /alternatives/sendgrid/ or /alternatives/postmark/. If you outgrew Mail-in-a-Box's single-server model and need multi-tenant + API, read /alternatives/mail-in-a-box/. If iRedMail's OS-native install feels dated and you want REST API + atomic updates, read /alternatives/iredmail/." }
					},
					{
						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "Vectis Mail vs Mailcow vs iRedMail vs Mail-in-a-Box — what is the difference?",
						"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "All four are self-hosted email platforms but they target different operators. Mailcow and iRedMail are mature multi-domain mail servers: Mailcow ships as Docker Compose, iRedMail installs OS-native. Mail-in-a-Box is one-command personal email sovereignty on a single Ubuntu VPS. Vectis Mail targets a fourth slot: API-first, declarative YAML config, atomic updates with rollback, and a 40+ endpoint REST API designed for agencies, SaaS, and multi-tenant operators." }
					},
					{
						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "Vectis Mail vs SendGrid vs Postmark — are these comparable products?",
						"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Comparable on the transactional API surface: sending API, inbound webhooks, analytics, domain-scoped keys all match. Not comparable on the operational model. SendGrid and Postmark are managed SaaS billed per email; Vectis Mail is self-hosted on your own VPS billed flat ($0 Starter / $39 USD Pro per tenant per month, unlimited volume). Cost crossover for Postmark vs Vectis Mail Pro is around 37K emails/month on the Postmark side. Vectis Mail also includes full IMAP/POP3 mailbox hosting; SendGrid and Postmark do not." }
					},
					{
						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "Is there a Vectis Mail alternative for Mailu, Modoboa, docker-mailserver, Mailgun, AWS SES, or Resend?",
						"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Not yet. The current five comparisons cover the highest-search-volume products in our market. Mailu, Modoboa, Poste.io, docker-mailserver, Mailgun, AWS SES, and Resend are on the public roadmap for the next batch of comparison pages. If you want one prioritised, contact us and we'll sequence the next set based on real reader demand." }
					}
				]
			}
		]
	})} />
</head>
<body class="marketing-page">
	<nav class="marketing-nav">
		<a href="/" class="logo"><img src="/brand/logos/vectis-mail-logo-white.webp" alt="Vectis Mail" width="181" height="34" /></a>
		<div>
			<a href="/features/">Features</a>
			<a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a>
			<a href="/alternatives/">Compare</a>
			<a href="/getting-started/">Docs</a>
			<a href="/notes/">Notes</a>
			<a href="/about/">About</a>
			<a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
		</div>
	</nav>

	<main>

	<section class="hero alt-hero">
		<div class="hero-badge">Compare · Side-by-side</div>
		<h1>Vectis Mail alternatives.<br/><span>Where each one fits.</span></h1>
		<p class="alt-lead">
			Each comparison below leads with where the other product wins, where Vectis Mail wins,
			and a realistic migration path. These are written
			by the team that runs Vectis Mail in production at validonx.com,
			pharlux.com, scrutique.com, and other Veltara Works infrastructure.
		</p>
		<div class="alt-meta">
			<span>Last updated <time datetime={dateModified}>13 May 2026</time></span>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" style="padding-top: 1.5rem;">
		<h2>Direct comparisons</h2>
		<p class="subtitle">Each page has a side-by-side table, a clear verdict, and a migration walk-through.</p>
		<div class="feature-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
			{live.map((a) => (
				<a href={a.href} class="feature-card alt-index-card">
					<h3>{a.title} &rarr;</h3>
					<p style="margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">{a.tagline}</p>
					<ul class="alt-index-bullets">
						{a.bullets.map((b) => (<li>{b}</li>))}
					</ul>
				</a>
			))}
		</div>
	</section>

	{upcoming.length > 0 && (
		<section class="section" style="padding-top: 1rem;">
			<h2>Coming soon</h2>
			<p class="subtitle">More comparisons being written. If there's a specific product you'd like us to cover, <a href="/contact/">let us know</a>.</p>
			<div class="feature-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
				{upcoming.map((a) => (
					<div class="feature-card" style="opacity: 0.7;">
						<h3>{a.title}</h3>
						<p>{a.tagline}</p>
					</div>
				))}
			</div>
		</section>
	)}

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
		<div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(400px, 1fr));">
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Which comparison should I read first?</h3>
				<p>Start with the page that matches what you're running today. Coming from Mailcow → <a href="/alternatives/mailcow/">vs Mailcow</a>. Paying SendGrid or Postmark per email → <a href="/alternatives/sendgrid/">vs SendGrid</a> or <a href="/alternatives/postmark/">vs Postmark</a>. Outgrew Mail-in-a-Box → <a href="/alternatives/mail-in-a-box/">vs Mail-in-a-Box</a>. iRedMail feels dated → <a href="/alternatives/iredmail/">vs iRedMail</a>.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Vectis Mail vs Mailcow vs iRedMail vs Mail-in-a-Box — what's different?</h3>
				<p>All four are self-hosted email platforms targeting different operators. Mailcow ships as Docker Compose, iRedMail installs OS-native, Mail-in-a-Box is one-command personal sovereignty on a single VPS. Vectis Mail targets a fourth slot: API-first, declarative YAML, atomic updates with rollback, and a 40+ endpoint REST API for agencies, SaaS, and multi-tenant operators.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Vectis Mail vs SendGrid vs Postmark — are these even comparable?</h3>
				<p>On the API surface, yes: sending API, inbound webhooks, analytics, domain-scoped keys all match. On the operational model, no. SendGrid and Postmark are managed SaaS billed per email; Vectis Mail is self-hosted on your own VPS, billed flat ($0 Starter / $39 USD Pro per tenant per month, unlimited volume). Cost crossover with Postmark sits around 37K emails/month. Vectis Mail also includes full IMAP/POP3 mailbox hosting; SendGrid and Postmark do not.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Is there a comparison for Mailu, docker-mailserver, Mailgun, AWS SES, or Resend?</h3>
				<p>Not yet. The current five cover the highest-search-volume products. Mailu, Modoboa, Poste.io, docker-mailserver, Mailgun, AWS SES, and Resend are on the roadmap for the next batch. Want one prioritised? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a> and we'll sequence the next set based on real reader demand.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" style="text-align: center;">
		<div class="hero-buttons">
			<a href="/getting-started/installation/" class="btn-primary">Install Vectis Mail</a>
			<a href="/pricing/" class="btn-secondary">View Pricing</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<p class="page-meta">Last updated <time datetime={dateModified}>13 May 2026</time></p>


	</main>

	<SiteFooter />
</body>
</html>
